load @/code/type/term
  find term

# The self type, the one primitive under all inductive types, and the bottom of the shared foundation with the kernel.
# A self type binds a value to its own type, so its members are the terms that inhabit a family applied to themselves.
# The self combinator names the fixed point of a family. Every later inductive type, the booleans, the naturals, the
# integers, the algebra tower, is a self type whose body states its own induction principle, so the trusted core stays
# tiny while expressing inductive and even inductive-inductive types, exactly what a self-hosting compiler needs for
# its own syntax tree. Nothing else is added as a primitive.
#
# The rules. Formation: a self type is well-formed when its body, given a value standing for the type itself, is a
# type. Introduction: a value inhabits the self type when it inhabits the body with itself substituted in. Elimination:
# a value of the self type may be used at the body with the value substituted in. Introduction and elimination are
# mutually inverse coercions the checker discharges by normalization.
form self-type
  link body, like term
